203. Code review: Is this MetricsTracker thread-safe?

   public class MetricsTracker {

       private final ConcurrentHashMap<String, LongAdder> pageViews =
               new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

       public void incrementView(String pageId) {
           pageViews.putIfAbsent(pageId, new LongAdder());
           pageViews.get(pageId).increment();
       }
   }

   1. ConcurrentHashMap makes map operations thread-safe.
   2. LongAdder supports efficient concurrent counter updates with less contention than a single AtomicLong in high-contention scenarios.
   3. I would simplify the code using computeIfAbsent().
   4. I would also handle null page IDs and consider memory growth if the number of unique pages is unlimited.

   Improved code:

   public void incrementView(String pageId) {
       pageViews.computeIfAbsent(
           pageId, key -> new LongAdder()
       ).increment();
   }

   To read the count:

   long count = pageViews.get(pageId).sum();

   Note: LongAdder.sum() is not an atomic snapshot while updates are happening.

